# AAP MCP → Copilot Studio (MCP wizard)

Generated: {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 }}

Use the **native MCP onboarding wizard** in Copilot Studio (recommended). Custom OpenAPI connectors are optional for DLP or multi-tenant publish scenarios.

## Prerequisites

- [Microsoft Copilot Studio](https://copilotstudio.microsoft.com) access
- **Generative orchestration** enabled on your agent ([docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/agent-extend-action-mcp))
- AAP MCP reachable over **HTTPS** with a valid certificate (no self-signed)
- Streamable HTTP transport ([docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/mcp-add-existing-server-to-agent))

## Authentication

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Type | Basic (API key in `Authorization` header) |
| Header | `Authorization` |
| Value | `Basic {{ basic_auth_token }}` |

⚠️ Include the `Basic ` prefix and a single space before the Base64 token.

## MCP server URLs

Register each toolset your deployment exposes (or the unified endpoint if supported):

| Toolset | URL |
|---------|-----|
| Unified | `{{ aap_mcp_base_url }}{{ aap_mcp_server_path }}` |
{% for toolset in aap_mcp_toolsets %}
| {{ toolset | replace('_', ' ') | title }} | `{{ aap_mcp_base_url }}/{{ toolset }}/mcp` |
{% endfor %}

## Steps (Copilot Studio UI)

1. Open [Copilot Studio](https://copilotstudio.microsoft.com) → your agent (**{{ copilot_agent_name }}**).
2. Confirm **Generative orchestration** is on (Settings).
3. Go to **Tools** → **Add a tool** → **MCP** (or use the MCP onboarding wizard).
4. Enter the MCP server URL (start with unified `{{ aap_mcp_server_path }}` or a toolset URL from the table above).
5. Configure authentication with the Basic header value above.
6. Save and test a prompt, e.g. *"List available Ansible job templates."*

## Verify from your workstation

```bash
curl -sk -X POST '{{ aap_mcp_base_url }}{{ aap_mcp_server_path }}' \
  -H 'Authorization: Basic {{ basic_auth_token }}' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"test","version":"1.0"}}}'
```

## Custom connector (optional)

If your tenant requires Power Platform connectors (DLP, published connector):

```bash
ansible-playbook playbooks/prepare-copilot-setup.yml --tags copilot_artifacts
```

See `SETUP-INSTRUCTIONS.txt` in `copilot-setup-artifacts/`.

